# WHAT HIS BUNKER HOLDS, BEFORE HE KNOWS (docs/story/UNDER_THE_STONES.md): down
# the hatch among the cast stones nearest where he woke -- No. 4, his -- and read
# through the real keys. The terminal is dark to a man who does not yet know the
# oldest machines take his passwords; the drawer under it and the board beside it
# are open from the first day. Each page is a press of `use` in front of the thing.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/bunker_words.tour --seed=4 --hour=15 --weather=clear:0
#
# 01 is the drawer (a shut page gives way to an open one at the same desk), 02 the
# terminal, dark, 03 the whiteboard, 04 the room again once the glass is put down.
# tours/bunker_woken.tour is the same terminal once he knows.
coast calm
near door:bunker
await door 5
press use
await inside:bunker 5
wait 1.0
tap lamp
wait 0.4

at slot:terminal
wait 0.4
press use
await knows:bunker_phones 4
wait 0.5
shot 01-two-phones-in-the-drawer with inside:bunker,tenant:his,reading
press use
wait 0.4

press use
await reading 4
wait 0.5
shot 02-the-terminal-dark-to-a-stranger with inside:bunker,tenant:his,reading
press use
wait 0.4

at slot:whiteboard
wait 0.4
press use
await knows:bunker_board 4
wait 0.5
shot 03-one-line-boxed-on-the-whiteboard with inside:bunker,reading
press use
wait 0.5
shot 04-the-work-room-again with inside:bunker
